Package: vds
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Jihong Min <hurryman2212@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: bluez, kmod, libc6, libbluetooth3, libdbus-1-3, libopus0, libstdc++6, libudev1
Recommends: logrotate
Suggests: pipewire, systemd, udev, wireplumber
Description: Virtual DualSense Bluetooth-to-USB bridge
 vDS exposes Bluetooth-connected DualSense-class controllers through a virtual
 USB controller so games and applications can use features normally available
 only over USB. Virtual controllers are plugged into the kernel's in-tree
 vhci_hcd (USB/IP) driver; no out-of-tree kernel module is needed. The package
 installs the userspace daemon, CLI, systemd unit, udev rule and a
 modules-load.d entry for vhci-hcd.
